Article 2 (Duties) The Armed Forces Transportation Command (hereinafter referred to as the "Command") shall perform the following duties: <Amended on Mar. 23, 2010>
1. Affairs concerning military transportation by rail and road;
2. Affairs concerning maritime transportation support and air transportation support for the Army and Air Force (in cooperation with the relevant service);
3. Affairs concerning wartime transportation plans;
4. Affairs concerning strategic transportation support for the armed forces, including coordination and control of the operation of civilian vessels and aircraft mobilized in wartime;
5. Affairs concerning the management of military movements by rail and road and support for escort duties;
6. Affairs concerning the operation of landing logistics through ports and coastal areas (in cooperation with the relevant service);
7. Affairs concerning the airlift of military supplies and equipment (in cooperation with the relevant service);
8. Establishment and operation of the Combined and Joint Transportation and Movement Headquarters;
9. Affairs concerning transportation support for overseas military deployments.
